{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1523005-can-embrace-result-in-failure-and-if-it-can-what-are-the-factors","id":1523005,"title":"Can Embrace result in failure and if it can, what are the factors?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-09-23T04:05:37-07:00","id":1523005,"title":"Can Embrace result in failure and if it can, what are the factors?","content":"I am relatively new to VTM lore and I have some questions regarding how can the Embrace fail (result in dead to-be-childer), if it can.<br /> Does the fail factor depend on the to-be-sire or to-be-childer?<br /> I am creating a low-willed character that can be easily manipulated by other person, that has some charisma or even just natural beauty in them. This character is not so intelligent either, so if the Embrace failure depends on to-be-childer's willpower (like will to live or strength of spirit) or mental strength, my character concept fails. If Embrace chance depends on to-be-sire, then I can keep my concept.\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28209-kaelharan","name":"Kaelharan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-23T04:22:19-07:00","id":1523006,"title":"","content":"Embrace can fail, but it's not mechanically defined what causes it to fail (unless we speak of Thinbloods, but that's a different problem). It's a narrative tool that exists to create drama and fear of what happens to someone you might need to become a vampire, and doesn't. Your character by dint of being a player character will be a vampire no matter what they are like.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-23T10:32:46-07:00","id":1523038,"title":"","content":"There is no real answer why an embrace will fail, just like why a Caitiff can come into existence and doesn't take on their parent clan's strengths &amp; weaknesses.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-23T15:18:24-07:00","id":1523051,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1523005-can-embrace-result-in-failure-and-if-it-can-what-are-the-factors?p=1523006#post1523006\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Embrace can fail, but it's not mechanically defined what causes it to fail (unless we speak of Thinbloods, but that's a different problem). It's a narrative tool that exists to create drama and fear of what happens to someone you might need to become a vampire, and doesn't. Your character by dint of being a player character will be a vampire no matter what they are like.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1523005-can-embrace-result-in-failure-and-if-it-can-what-are-the-factors?p=1523038#post1523038\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is no real answer why an embrace will fail, just like why a Caitiff can come into existence and doesn't take on their parent clan's strengths &amp; weaknesses.</div> </div> </div> </div>Going by the good, old meta, what few rules do exist for the embrace (at least last time i checked, if i missed anything on V20 or V5, people are free to correct me) do not involve any form of dice-rolling, making the matter of what might be considered a failure of the embrace utterly subjective, in and out of character perspective both.<br /> <br /> Is a Caitiff being labeled as a failure correct if, clan identifiers notwithstanding, it's as potent as any other childe of the same sire? If belonging to a clan is &quot;the right/natural way&quot; for all kindred, yes.<br /> But by that logic wouldn't bloodlines be just as much of a failures in a way?<br /> And for belonging to a clan to be &quot;the right/natural way&quot; would it not mean <b>that all kindred started on them</b> and there was never a 2nd or 1st generation above/before the Clan Founders?<br /> <br /> (I can see that kind of discussion getting inconvenient and messy <b>fast</b> in some elysia....)<br /> <br /> <br /> Can Thinbloods be considered failures if the person drained <i>did</i> return as an undead thing that feeds on blood?<br /> They are different from most kindred in capacities and ceiling power for sure, but so aren't most kindred from those in the 4-7th generations? One might point out that <b>most kindred</b>, those belonging to the 8-13th generations, are the weird ones for the extended consistency in power level, from that perspective.<br /> <br /> And that without going into the utterly confusing rigmarole of different takes and systems that have been used to portray thinbloods from Revised to V20 and then V5.<br /> <br /> Or the fact that the conditions that cause one to rise as thin-blood may change with time or be temporary, if not both, as seen from conflicting bits like mentions of 12-13th gen vampires frequently showing thinblood qualities in VtDA/DA:V, the appearance of 16th gen neonates in BJD (and V5 too, i think), <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Jenna_Cross\" target=\"_blank\">Jenna Cross</a> being thin-blood even though she's 11th generation and the childe of Smiling Jack, a Brujah notorious for illegal embraces, but also for how these childer all too frequently take after his blood, unlike her.<br /> <br /> And oh yeah, we also have <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Okulos\" target=\"_blank\">Okulos</a>, who apparently was labeled a thin-blood back at the time of his embrace but seems to have no issue producing childer or being treated as an equal or near equal in a circle of acquaintances involving individuals like <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Cuthbert_Beckett\" target=\"_blank\">Beckett</a>, <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Hesha_Ruhadze\" target=\"_blank\">Hesha</a>, <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Aisling_Sturbridge\" target=\"_blank\">Aisling Sturbridge</a> and <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Anatole\" target=\"_blank\">Anatole</a> among others.<br /> <br /> (To boot, <a href=\"https://www.ebay.com/itm/334226742382\" target=\"_blank\">His </a>VtES card implies he would be 8-10th generation, depending on how one goes with such rough conversions, what has varied over time)\u200b<br /> <br /> <br /> Anyway, my main point is, everything is an utterly royal mess - and truth be told, i'd say it's pretty much by design, every side is claiming whatever for any number of logical, irrational or utterly twisted reasons better suit them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 10-18-2023, 03:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-18T04:45:09-07:00","id":1524221,"title":"","content":"From a Deus ex machina perspective, the Embrace must work. People with true faith or some hardcore Spirit, Mind or Life spheres may avoid it, but mostly they're just embraced.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27825-mrdrika","name":"MrDrika","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27825_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"64"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-18T09:06:01-07:00","id":1524224,"title":"","content":"The Embrace can fail in that the Cainite in question screws things up and the target dies instead of being turned. I figure that emptying someone of blood and then make them ingest a bit of your blood before they have died may not have a 100% success rate, in particular for an inexperienced Cainite. Hence a fair degree of first, second or third time attemtps at the Embrace would in my opinion likely result in a dead human and not a new Cainite.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-18T12:50:19-07:00","id":1524232,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrDrika</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1523005-can-embrace-result-in-failure-and-if-it-can-what-are-the-factors?p=1524221#post1524221\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From a Deus ex machina perspective, the Embrace must work. People with true faith or some hardcore Spirit, Mind or Life spheres may avoid it, but mostly they're just embraced.</div> </div> </div> </div>Gnosis too - from what i remember in old books, any attempt to embrace a Garou (and apparently Fera in general) results in certain death - instant and painless if you roll successfully, drawn-out &amp; excruciating otherwise - unless they <b>botch</b> a reflexive Gnosis roll, what results in an Abomination.<br /> <br /> (If the same applies to Fomori, Kami or other spirit-possessed people, no idea but hypothetically possible, i guess)<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gurkhal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1523005-can-embrace-result-in-failure-and-if-it-can-what-are-the-factors?p=1524224#post1524224\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Embrace can fail in that the Cainite in question screws things up and the target dies instead of being turned. I figure that emptying someone of blood and then make them ingest a bit of your blood before they have died may not have a 100% success rate, in particular for an inexperienced Cainite. Hence a fair degree of first, second or third time attemtps at the Embrace would in my opinion likely result in a dead human and not a new Cainite.</div> </div> </div> </div>Weird thing is, the timespan where a person is &quot;embraceable&quot; might be longer than we give credit for, since a lot of &quot;impulse embraces&quot; seem to be a sort of reaction to salvage already dried out frenzy victims. Less seconds and possibly more like minutes before oxygen deprivation damage kicks in or somesuch. Thought i'll be the first to admit that is me over-analyzing the back &amp; forth between fluff &amp; mechanics.\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-19T03:31:29-07:00","id":1524263,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gurkhal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1523005-can-embrace-result-in-failure-and-if-it-can-what-are-the-factors?p=1524224#post1524224\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Embrace can fail in that the Cainite in question screws things up and the target dies instead of being turned. I figure that emptying someone of blood and then make them ingest a bit of your blood before they have died may not have a 100% success rate, in particular for an inexperienced Cainite. Hence a fair degree of first, second or third time attemtps at the Embrace would in my opinion likely result in a dead human and not a new Cainite.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bIf I remember right, there was a Ravnos (?) (or Malkavian?) fiction in the Revised core book where a Kindred worried he'd given the blood a little too late and just kept waiting for his lover to rise. Just waiting. Waiting...<br /> So the Embrace tho' not stated rarely if ever works on some one who is dead more than a few minutes<br /> Or if the vitae was out from the vampire's body for too long - and not preserved some supernatural ways - usually it has to be done immediately.<br /> <br /> And of course there is the possibility.... well, the vampie simply had no idea how to Embrace.<br /> I mean it is not something many could recall or the Sire should/would included in the &quot;What you must know&quot; lessons.<br /> Actually I think many Sire proposefully will not tell their Child (or outright lies to them how to do it) to avoid any potential Tradition breach - if the Fledgeling don't know how to Embrace, the chance she in panic after her first kill tries to &quot;save&quot; the victim and commit a &quot;crime&quot; lessen greatly - and following what you could read in books, myths and see TV? Good luck with those.<br /> A few or none of those would end up in an Embrace\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}